            </section>
            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 77-year-old male patient, who presented with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he exhibited increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation consistent with COPD without signs of pneumonia. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests revealed mild systemic inflammation. The patient was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Pulse oximetry was monitored continuously throughout the stay. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. Patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation self-management was provided prior to discharge. Please ensure follow-up spirometry and continued optimisation of maintenance therapy. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
